review_comments.body:
Claude suggested the following.

```
Put the wrap rule in one place. "Rethrow a ClosedChannelException, otherwise wrap in FileReadException" appears three times: FileRecords.fileSize, and size() and read() in SslTransportLayer. A static helper keeps the rule in one place:


// In FileReadException
public static IOException ofReadFailure(long position, IOException e) {
    // A file closed concurrently, by a deletion or a shutdown, says nothing about the medium
    return e instanceof ClosedChannelException ? e : new FileReadException(position, e);
}
...
} catch (IOException e) {
    throw FileReadException.ofReadFailure(pos, e);
}
```

